<main><section class="page-head"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">About</div><h1>Research discipline, applied to practical machine learning.</h1><p class="section-lead">I use data analysis and machine learning to solve real-world problems where technical results need to translate into practical value.</p></div></section><section><div class="container content"><h2>How I work</h2><p>I care about defining the real decision, checking what information would actually be available at prediction time, validating under conditions that resemble deployment, and being explicit about limitations.</p><div class="callout">The standard I aim for is simple: a result should be credible enough to defend, useful enough to act on, and clear enough to explain.</div><h2>What I work on</h2><ul><li>Applied machine learning and ranking problems</li><li>NLP and stance classification</li><li>Time-series modelling and predictive maintenance</li><li>Model validation, leakage control and interpretation</li></ul><p><a class="cta" href="/case-studies">View case studies</a></p></div></section></main>
